[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4443807656","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119409#issuecomment-4443807656","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119409","id":4443807656,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCN8fqA","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T17:49:32Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T17:49:32Z","body":"While I do agree this is better, it introduces an inconsistency. Now the way the default value is presented in the overview is way too different (`[default: 1.0]`), as if it's conceptually referring to something else.\r\n\r\nMy suggestion is to stick to just values for both the overview and over the descriptions. Reason being that the meaning of \"*that gray value on the side*\" can be easily inferred over time, given enough familiarity with the editor.\r\nIn the worst case scenario, a hover tooltip could be added for clarification, but we can see later. I don't think it's necessary.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/iss